Mechanical Enclosure
The mechanical enclosure for this project was designed by Jordan Lin.

Jordan designed a custom SolidWorks casing around the metronome PCB and supporting plate hardware. The enclosure was developed to securely package the electronics while maintaining access to the PCB and allowing the board to be removed when required.

Enclosure Features
Custom tapered SolidWorks casing
100 mm × 90 mm PCB mounting cavity
Separate 71 mm × 55 mm secondary plate cavity
Wiring clearance and pass-through features
M3 screw pivot system
Two movable PCB retaining rails
Mechanical rail stops
SolidWorks assembly testing to verify rail movement and PCB accessibility

The original retention concept used a single rail across the PCB. During assembly testing, this was found to obstruct access to PCB controls. The system was redesigned to use separate top and bottom retaining rails, allowing the PCB to remain secure while keeping its controls accessible.
